/* book Worked example 2: Q: The same cantilever carries a uniform downward load w = 0.8 N/mm (800 N/m) instead of the tip load. Compute the deflected shape at five stations with a short program, and check the tip against the closed form u = w L⁴ Ixy/(8 E D), v = −w L⁴ Iyy/(8 E D).
   1. Mx = w(L − z)²/2 at station z (tension at the top), My = 0; the program turns it into u″ and v″ at 1 mm steps.
   2. It integrates each curvature twice by the trapezium rule from zero slope and deflection at the root.
   3. The tip values match the closed form, and u/v = −Ixy/Iyy = −1.5 at every station.
   Answer: Tip deflection 15.23 mm sideways and 10.16 mm down, matching the closed form. */
