/* book: lead: An aircraft section is mostly thin sheet: skins about 1 to 3 mm thick, webs and stringer flanges a few millimetres. Thin walls allow big simplifications. The stress hardly changes across the thickness, so each wall can be drawn as its mid-line with a thickness t, and terms in t³ can be dropped. This chapter sets out those approximations, gives the sums that turn walls and stringers into Ixx, Iyy a */
