/* book Worked example 2: Q: Find Ixx, Iyy and Ixy of the Z-section used in the unsymmetrical bending and deflection chapters: web 100 mm (vertical), top flange 50 mm in +x, bottom flange 50 mm in −x, all 2 mm thick.
   1. The section is antisymmetric about the web centre, so the centroid is at the middle of the web. Each flange has a = 100 mm²; the web has a = 200 mm².
   2. Ixx: web own term 2 × 100³/12 = 166,667; flanges 2 × 100 × 50² = 500,000 (their own Ixx,0 is zero). Ixx = 666,667 mm⁴.
   3. Iyy: web contributes nothing; each flange has own term 2 × 50³/12 = 20,833 plus 100 × 25² = 62,500. Iyy = 2 × 83,333 = 166,667 mm⁴.
   4. Ixy: top flange centroid (25, 50) gives 100 × 25 × 50 = 125,000; bottom flange (−25, −50) gives another +125,000; the web's centroid is at the origin. Ixy = +250,000 mm⁴.
   Answer: Ixx = 666,667 mm⁴, Iyy = 166,667 mm⁴ and Ixy = +250,000 mm⁴, the values used for the Z-section stresses and deflections. */
